{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/425208-elders-and-mythic-werewolves-hunt-what","id":425208,"title":"Elders and Mythic Werewolves Hunt what?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-02T08:05:27-08:00","id":425208,"title":"Elders and Mythic Werewolves Hunt what?","content":"Hello all once again,<br /> I'm curious as to what elder and high PU werewolves do in your games and stories. What kind of shenanigans do high powered Uratha get into? Are they totemic for younger pups? How do they deal with spending so much time in the shadow? What kind of quests and goals do high powered Wolves have? How does it change from a low PU wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3905-llewyd42","name":"Llewyd42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T08:37:00-08:00","id":425246,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in seeing the responses to this too. I know a lot of people seem to like the milestone gifts, so I figure at least some have gotten to the point where they got them in game. My own games never got that high, and in the games I ran the three powerful werewolves were mostly antagonists. They had cults and organizations. Have, I guess is more appropriate since one of them has never been stopped.<br /> <br /> It looks like second edition might expand on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T09:01:57-08:00","id":425286,"title":"","content":"They hunt (obviously - all werewolves do). They interact with the PCs - because otherwise, what's the point of them existing, narratively - by giving them work, making things harder and easier for them, as needed by the story.<br /> <br /> They also exemplify many of the horror stories and legends of werewolves, existing both as shining examples, and, more often, cautionary tales of what the PCs might become one day. If you've been a werewolf for a long time, you won't be quite right in the head. Both the strong attunement to an auspice, and, by proxy, the mad moon; and the closeness of the tribal totem influence a werewolf, usually by making him less human. Elders are so very far away from humanity. Think weird, spirit-like bans that make sense only to them; opinions and outlooks that cannot easily be justified or explained, because you haven't been there and you haven't seen and experienced what they have.<br /> <br /> In a word, high-powered werewolves are less people and more archetypes - icons, if you will. Old Man Wolf. The chimera, so adept at taking on various shapes that he (it?) can't even remember what his own, original form was like. The wolf-witch, holding entire entourages of shadowy beings in her thrall. The warrior of the people, sleeping under a mountain, until it's time to arise and go hunting again. That sort of thing. Think epic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 03-02-2015, 01:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T22:03:14-08:00","id":427447,"title":"","content":"In addition to what Christian said, if you're asking from a player character perspective:<br /> <br /> Think epic, as Christian said. Elder werewolves no longer deal with the same paltry problems that plague lesser hunters. Their effective spirit Rank makes them terrible threats to less powerful spirits, and the spirits know it. You stalk the Shadow as an apex predator, threatened only by other apex predators: major spirits and forces capable of affecting whole regions. Your physical might is so great that no natural land animal can withstand you, nor pose any serious threat. You don't hunt the minor spirits anymore. You don't measure your territory in city blocks. You measure it in miles, in whole counties or maybe more. Your hunts take you deeper into the <i>Hisil </i>than others dare go, because that is where need drives you to go. You go in search of godlike spirits' bans, or banes to use against the lords of the spirit world, to uncover ancient secrets, to find pieces of the spirit world once thought lost.<br /> <br /> Emphasize the strangeness. Embrace it when you roleplay your character. You're old, powerful, and have long since left humanity behind. You have bans and beyond that, the strange habits and beliefs that develop over years or decades of hunting alien entities from a shadowy realm. Your connection to an insane moon goddess has given you visions of things no human can understand. Also, you've killed dozens or hundreds of people, monsters, even conceptual embodiments. The wolf must hunt. This holds true at every level of werewolf life, but for elders, it takes on new meaning. You sometimes literally <i>hunt</i> meanings, and ancient terrors, monstrosities about which the world remains blissfully ignorant.<br /> <br /> When your characters go to the physical world, emphasize how that world is now alien to them. It doesn't make sense the way it once did. The Shadow makes more sense, and the strange ways of the spirits are more logical to you than these human creatures and their world of glass and concrete. It's difficult to rein in the super-predator that lurks within your heart. You bristle under human laws, because they don't apply to you. Human concerns mean nothing to ageless killers who hunt spirit lords for a living. What use is money? What use is political power, except among the courts of the Shadow? Neither disease nor mortal weapons kill you.<br /> <br /> All of this adds up to make for very mythic and very alien stories. You are far removed from humanity, and yes, you are powerful, but that's part of why. Try to make it feel like you're at this higher level by downplaying things that concern mortals and younger werewolves. Play up the strangeness in the shadows. Embrace the fact that such werewolves are living legends, and their stories take on a more epic tone. Above all, make sure to have fun with it!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}